<title>NETHERLANDS: New Euroflour president appointed.</title>
<headline>New Euroflour president appointed.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ingid Kauderer has been named president of the European Association of Flour Exporters for two-year term, the Brussels-based organisation said on Friday.</p>
<p>Kauderer, a director of Menaba Meel BV where she is responsible for wheat and rye purchases, succeeds Bernard Valhuis of the Soufflet Group, who has finished a three-year term as president, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Euroflour said its purpose was to contribute to the elaboration, implementation and safeguarding of a milling policy within the European Union and to defend the interests of European flour exporters in the international arena.</p>
<p>&quot;The coming years will pose formidable challenges for our industry. The continuing reform of the Common Agriculatural Policy, the enlargement of the EU, the major changes being witnessed at international level with the implementation of the Marrakesh (WTO) Agreement and the U.S. Fair Trading Act are the major developments to be addressed,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
